{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:2948ef2dfab5201a","name":"Bantha","source":{"id":"source:reference-2948ef2dfab5201a","title":"Bantha","revision":16129,"timestamp":"2024-08-18T00:56:20Z","sha256":"85f9bc0f458f45300cccc21fac223fda3f5ae0d891620050cfcfd138d5602a64","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=16129","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Bantha&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-2948ef2dfab5201a","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unknown Regions Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unknown_Regions_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Perhaps the most adaptable herbivores in the galaxy, Banthas are found on numerous worlds and are so well known that their name is used in a plethora of proverbs, sayings, and children's stories. Several fringe religions see the Bantha as a divine messenger. Banthas can survive in most environmental extremes, and are able to go without food or water for several weeks. Although many subspecies have adapted to the peculiarities of their environments, most Banthas have large, curving horns and long, shaggy fur.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Banthas are commonly used as transportation and as beasts of burden. Their meat and hides are highly prized, particularly by the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tusken Raiders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tusken_Raiders"}," of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tatooine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tatooine","referenceId":"reference:a1b911e88e4876e1"},", who use the beasts extensively.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Banthas Across the Galaxy"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The Bantha serves as an archetypical mount and pack animal anywhere in the galaxy. The Bantha statistics below represent the baseline for the common Bantha. Gamemasters should feel free to alter that statistics block to make the Bantha better fit the environment in which it is found.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["As examples, the dune Banthas of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tatooine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tatooine","referenceId":"reference:a1b911e88e4876e1"}," would have the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Desert Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Desert_Beast"}," trait, and the white-furred Banthas of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nelvaan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nelvaan","referenceId":"reference:fa265d5d5a02f9bd"}," would have the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Arctic Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Arctic_Beast"}," trait. The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kashyyyk"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kashyyyk","referenceId":"reference:0886d73261c13472"}," grayclimber subspecies would exchange the Trample attack for the Expert Climber quality. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Aquatic Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Aquatic_Beast"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Subterranean Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Subterranean_Beast"}," Banthas might be waiting out there in the galaxy for your intrepid group of explorers to discover.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Bantha Statistics (CL 2)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Huge ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +1; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +1\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 8 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"]